ry  University that said wearing  a mask will help stop the spread of this  virus and yet governor Kemp went to a  small university and I state to get the  opinion that he wanted I think you could  probably locate the president if you  wanted to hand him that citation but I'm  curious about the perspective of  businesses the governor says he's  bringing this lawsuit on behalf of  businesses and people who are looking  for jobs want to stay employed what's  your response to that do you think the  mandatory mask requirement and your  rollback to phase one hurts the economy  there in Georgia absolutely not again  Reading Is Fundamental are  recommendations going back to phase one  were advisory voluntary recommendations  and so to be sued based upon the issuing  voluntary advisory recommendations  really is just a waste of taxpayer money  in our state we don't have appropriate  contact tracing we don't have adequate  testing in our state I personally waited  eight days for results and by the time I  got my results when we I was tested it  was one person in my household who was  asymptomatic and positive eight days  later myself and my husband were then  yeah positive for Kovac 19 and my  husband being very ill so I think a  better use of taxpayer money would be to  expand testing and contact tracing in  our state and not to waste it on suing  me personally in our Atlanta City  Council personally simply because we're  trying to save lives in our city do you  think the governor's positions is  costing lives I absolutely think that  it's costing you think the governor's  position is killing people there in  Georgia that's a pretty bow  we have over 31 we have over 3,100  Georgians who have died of kovat 19 I  believe our numbers as of yesterday were  over 130,000 who have tested positive  many are senior citizens many are in  minority communities and so I think that  when you are reckless as the governor  has been when you disregard science as  the governor has done then 